{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneC2QDimTranspose","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneC2QDimTranspose","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneC2DimTranspose","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.qPlancherelWeight_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.qPlancherelWeight_conj","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2QDimTranspose.lean#L203-L212","doc":"**Keystone necessary condition C2 (weight level): `W_λ = W_{λ′}`.**  The q-Plancherel weight is\ntranspose-invariant — the direct corollary of `qDim_conj` (the q-dimension `d_q` is transpose-\ninvariant) and `sz_conj` (`|λ′| = |λ|`, so the `[n]_q!` normaliser is unchanged).  This is the\nkeystone's chirality-blindness of the weight, now Lean-proved for the genuine q-weight at any real\n`q` (no fit, no `q₀`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.qPlancherelWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.qPlancherelWeight","kind":"def","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2QDimTranspose.lean#L197-L201","doc":"The **q-Plancherel weight** of a partition `λ ⊢ n`: `W_λ = d_q(λ)² / [n]_q!`.  This is the\nquantity whose conjugation symmetry `W_λ = W_{λ′}` is the s5-so3 keystone's necessary condition\nC2 (the weight is *chirality-blind*). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.qDim_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.qDim_conj","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2QDimTranspose.lean#L167-L193","doc":"**C2 — the genuine q-version: the q-hook-length dimension is transpose-invariant**,\n`d_q(λ) = d_q(λ')`, hence the q-Plancherel weight `W_λ = d_q(λ)²/[n]_q!` satisfies `W_λ = W_{λ'}`\n(the s5-so3 keystone's necessary condition C2 — the weight is chirality-blind).\n\n`qDim q λ = [|λ|]_q! / ∏_c [h_c]_q`.  Both inputs are transpose-invariant: the size `|λ|` by\n`sz_conj`, and the `qBracket`-weighted hook product by `qHookProd_conj` (rewriting each genuine\ncell's `Partition.hookLength` to the merged `colLen`-hook via `hookLength_eq`, on both `conj l`\n— sorted by `conj_sorted` — and `l`).  So the q-dimension is too. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.qDim_eq_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.qDim_eq_prod","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2QDimTranspose.lean#L158-L165","doc":"**`qDim` as a double `Finset.prod`.** Unfold the nested `foldl` denominator into a `Finset`\ndouble product, with the inner row-length bound normalised to `l.getD i 0` (`getQ_getD`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.foldl_mul_range","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.foldl_mul_range","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2QDimTranspose.lean#L148-L156","doc":"A multiplicative `foldl` over `range n` is the `Finset.prod` (product analog of the additive\n`list_range_map_sum`, but written directly on the `foldl` shape `qDim` uses). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.getQ_getD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.getQ_getD","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2QDimTranspose.lean#L143-L146","doc":"`(l[i]?).getD 0 = l.getD i 0` — the inner `qDim` row-length bound, normalised (agrees both\nin range, where `get? = some`, and out of range, where both are the default `0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.conj_sorted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.conj_sorted","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2QDimTranspose.lean#L134-L141","doc":"The merged conjugate `conj l` is itself weakly decreasing: its rows are the column lengths\n`colLen l j`, which decrease in `j` (`colLen_antitone`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.colLen_antitone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.colLen_antitone","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2QDimTranspose.lean#L123-L132","doc":"`colLen` is antitone in the column index `j`: wider columns sit at the left.  (Each row\nindicator `[j < λ_k]` only shrinks as `j` grows.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.hookLength_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.hookLength_eq","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2QDimTranspose.lean#L107-L119","doc":"**Bridge 2.** `Partition.hookLength l i j` equals the merged `colLen`-hook\n`(λ_i − j) + (colLen j − i) − 1` for a genuine cell of a weakly-decreasing partition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.leg_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.leg_count","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2QDimTranspose.lean#L82-L105","doc":"For a weakly-decreasing partition with `λ_i > j` (so cell `(i,j)` exists), the leg count\n`#{i' > i : λ_{i'} > j}` equals `colLen l j − (i+1)`: the first `i+1` rows all exceed `j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.conjugate_eq_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.conjugate_eq_conj","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2QDimTranspose.lean#L71-L78","doc":"**Bridge 1.** The `QPartitionCombinatorics` conjugate equals the merged `colLen`-conjugate on a\nweakly-decreasing partition: same range (`maxPart = headD`) and definitionally-equal map function\n(`(l.filter (· > j)).length = colLen l j`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.maxPart_eq_headD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.maxPart_eq_headD","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2QDimTranspose.lean#L59-L69","doc":"For a weakly-decreasing partition, `Partition.maxPart l = λ_1` (the head). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.foldl_max_eq_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.foldl_max_eq_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2QDimTranspose.lean#L52-L57","doc":"`foldl Nat.max a t = a` when every element of `t` is `≤ a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.qHookProd_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.qHookProd_conj","kind":"theorem","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2QDimTranspose.lean#L27-L48","doc":"**The `qBracket`-weighted hook product is transpose-invariant** (reusable core, ℝ).\n`∏_c [h_c]_q (λ') = ∏_c [h_c]_q (λ)`, with the hook in the merged `colLen` model.  Proof: identical\nto `prodHooks_conj` with `qBracket q (·)` wrapping the hook — the conjugate's hook at `(r,c)` equals\n`λ`'s hook at `(c,r)` (`colLen_conj` + arm/leg commute), and `cell_fubini_prod` (at `M = ℝˣ`-style\nmultiplicative `ℝ`) matches the cell sets. ","signatureChunk":0}]}